z preposition can indicate source as well as membership within a class.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "The phrase 'ten thousand years' may denote a vast appointed period of punishment; the wording is kept literal from the Ge'ez.", "reason": "cultural_note"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "The closing phrase is literally 'the number of the days of their sins,' preserving the text's image of punishment measured out according to their transgression.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "d", "text": "Or 'the ten thousand years'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}, {"marker": "e", "text": "Or 'These are among the stars that transgressed'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 21:7", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ወእምህየ፡ ሖርኩ፡ ካልአ፡ መካነ፡ እምዝ፡ ዘይገርም፡ ወርኢኩ፡ ግብረ፡ ግሩመ፤ እሳት፡ ዐቢይ፡ በህየ፡ ዘይነድድ፡ ወያንበለብል፡ ወመምተርተ፡ ቦቱ፡ መካኑ፡ እስከ፡ ቀላይ፡ ፍጹም፡ አዕማደ፡ እሳት፡ ዐበይተ፡ ዘይወርዶሙ፡ ወኢእምጣኖ፡ ወኢዕበዮ፡ አክሀልኩ፡ ነጽሮ፡ ወስእነኩ፡ [ነጽሮ፡] ዐይኖ።", "language": "Geez", "pages": [92], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "bounded_primary_scan_candidate_not_approved", "note": "Recovered from sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch21.txt via tools/enoch/verse_parser.py | Dillmann 1851 chapter OCR exists for chapter 21, but verse-aligned extraction is not yet implemented in this prompt builder."}, "translation": {"text": "And from there I went to another place[a], more terrible than this, and I saw a fearful work: a great fire was there, burning and blazing, and the place had a cleft reaching to the abyss, full of great pillars of fire descending; neither its measure nor its size was I able to see[c][b], and I was not able to look at it.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "The clause about the place being split downward is difficult in the Ge'ez. 'Cleft reaching to the abyss' represents a cautious rendering of a fissure or chasm extending to extreme depth.", "reason": "textual_variant"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "Or 'I was not able to discern its measure or its magnitude.' The point is Enoch's inability to comprehend the dimensions of what he sees.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "Or 'with great pillars of fire descending'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 21:8", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ውእተ፡ ጊዜ፡ እቤ፡ አፎ፡ ግሩም፡ ዝንቱ፡ መካን፡ ወሕሙም፡ ለነጽሮ።", "language": "Geez", "pages": [92], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "bounded_primary_scan_candidate_not_approved", "note": "Recovered from sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch21.txt via tools/enoch/verse_parser.py | Dillmann 1851 chapter OCR exists for chapter 21, but verse-aligned extraction is not yet implemented in this prompt builder."}, "translation": {"text": "And at that time I said[a], “How terrible this place is[c][b], and grievous to behold.”", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "The wording is somewhat difficult in the Ethiopic witness. The line is rendered here as a speech formula followed by Enoch's reaction to the place; some translators smooth 'my mouth' to 'I said.'", "reason": "textual_variant"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "Or 'fearsome and painful to look upon.'", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "Or 'my mouth spoke, saying, “This place is terrible'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 21:9", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ውእተ፡ ጊዜ፡ አውሥአኒ፡ ኡርኤል፡ ፩እምቅዱሳን፡ መላእክት፡ እንዘ፡ ምስሌየ፡ ሀሎ፡ ወይቤለኒ፡ ሄኖክ፡ ምንት፡ ፍርሃትከ፡ ከመዝ፡ ወድንጋጼከ፡ ወአውሣእኩ፡ በእንተዝ፡ ግሩም፡ መካን፡ ወቅድመ፡ ገጹ፡ *ለዝ፡ ሕማም፡፡", "language": "Geez", "pages": [92, 94], "confidence": "medium", "validation": "bounded_primary_scan_candidate_not_approved", "note": "Recovered from sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch21.txt via tools/enoch/verse_parser.py | Dillmann 1851 chapter OCR exists for chapter 21, but verse-aligned extraction is not yet implemented in this prompt builder."}, "translation": {"text": "And at that time Uriel, one of the holy angels who was with me, answered me and said, “Enoch, why are you so afraid and trembling?” And I answered, “Because of this terrifying place and the sight of this suffering.”[a]", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "The closing expression speaks of being before the face/appearance of this pain or suffering. Sight is a contextual rendering; it does not specify a mechanism of torment. The older clipped record incorrectly placed the question and answer beyond this verse.", "reason": "textual_uncertainty"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 21:10", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "language": "Geez", "text": "ወይቤለኒ፡ ዝመካን፡ ቤተ፡ ሞቅሖሙ፡ ለመላእክት፡ ወህየ፡ ይትአሐዙ፡ እስከ፡ ለዓለም።", "pages": [94], "validation": "bounded_primary_scan_candidate_not_approved"}, "translation": {"text": "And he said to me, “This place is the prison of the angels, and here they will be held forever.”[a]", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "The selected Geʿez names angels as the occupants and expresses extended duration. This line is not a claim about the human souls described in chapter 22.", "reason": "scope_disclosure"}]}}]
