    {
      "reference": "1 Enoch 21:2",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "reason": "Printed p.52/PDF90 reads ስርርተ, not ሱርርተ, and ends ወ*ግሩም, without the additional final ም. The English is supportable, but apparatus note 30 identifies an editorial emendation in the clause rendered 'unformed'; this should not be represented as an uncomplicated manuscript reading.",
      "suggested_text": "And there I saw a fearful work: I saw neither the heavens above nor the firmly founded earth, but a place unformed[a] and terrible.",
      "footnote_changes": "Add [a] after 'unformed': 'This follows Charles’s printed critical text. On p.52, note 30 identifies an emendation in this clause and compares Greek ἀκατασκεύαστον, “unformed/unprepared.” The Greek comparison and editorial correction are not independent Ethiopic manuscript confirmation.'",
      "suggested_source_text": "*ወበህየ፡ ርኢኩ፡ ግብረ፡ ግሩመ፤ ርኢኩ፡ ወአሰማየ፡ ላዕለ፡ ወአምድረ፡ ስርርተ፡ አላ፡ መካነ፡ ዘአኮ፡ ድልወ፡ ወ*ግሩም።"
    },
    {
      "reference": "1 Enoch 21:3",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "reason": "The submitted source includes the continuation onto printed p.54/PDF92 and preserves †ኅቡረ†. However, 'in it' obscures the more literal 'upon/above it,' and both relevant notes are incorrectly attached to 'mountains.' Apparatus p.52 note 37 treats the obelized word as a textual problem and discusses conjectural Greek transmission, not merely interchangeable synonyms. Page 54 note 1 also identifies a Greek-assisted emendation in the fire clause.",
      "suggested_text": "And there I saw seven stars of heaven, bound above it[a], together[b], like great mountains and burning in fire[c].",
      "footnote_changes": "Replace the existing notes. [a] after 'above it': 'Literally “upon/above it”; the referent should not be expanded into an otherwise unspecified structure.' [b] after 'together': 'Charles prints †ኅቡረ† as problematic. “Together” provisionally represents the printed reading. His discussion on p.52, note 37 includes proposed explanations involving Greek transmission; these are conjectures, not established Ethiopic variants meaning “clustered.”' [c] after 'fire': 'The continuation belongs to verse 3. On p.54, note 1 Charles identifies an emendation with Greek καὶ ἐν, “and in.”' Remove the speculative heavenly-beings note or reserve it for separately identified interpretation.",
      "suggested_source_text": ""
    },
    {
